{
  "case": "due2-shared-nodes",
  "source": "due2-native: a permission, a duty, and a constraint that two policies share (due2-workflows.md §4, decisions/0036, decisions/0050)",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "No origin: the case is due2-native, and every verdict is derived by hand. ex:outsideEU, ex:councilApproval, and ex:readCatalogue are each one node that both policies state; each policy states them in full, as W1 normalises each policy alone and the two descriptions must agree (due2-workflows.md §4, decisions/0036). Policy B adds two edges of its own, ex:browse below odrl:read and ex:signOff below ex:approve, and they widen only policy B's entries (decisions/0050): scenarios 7 to 9 show that. Until #157, clingo-i kept one finding per node, so scenarios 7 to 9 declined as read apart by their policies (clingo-i at d34d6d4). ex:councilApproval has no deadline and no recurrence, so sotw.activation is empty. A case could not give activation per policy anyway: sotw.activation is one instant per duty IRI, for every entry of the duty (conformance/README.md, sotw.activation).",
  "prefixes": {
    "ex": "https://example.org/"
  },
